TheWrap revealed what the canceled «Monsters, Inc.» sequel could have been like:

• Mike would’ve gotten married;  
• Sulley would’ve been promoted and taken over the company;  
• An older Boo would’ve returned to the main characters’ lives, kicking off an entirely new story.

The script was written nearly 15 years ago, but after Disney acquired Pixar, the project was scrapped. Instead, the studio opted to produce the prequel — «Monsters University».

